{"name":"Bittersweet Shimmer","hex":"#bf4f51","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bittersweet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Both bitter and sweet.","Expressing contrasting emotions of pain and pleasure."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Bittersweet nightshade (Solanum dulcamara).","Bittersweetness."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bittersweet"},{"term":"shimmer","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To shine tremulously or intermittently; to gleam faintly.","Of a mass of bees: to move their abdomens in a coordinated manner so as to produce a shimmering wave effect, thought to deter predators."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A faint or veiled and tremulous gleam or shining.","A measure of the irregularities in the loudness of a particular pitch over time."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shimmer"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shades of red","blocks":[{"text":"Varieties of the color red may differ in hue, chroma, lightness, or in two or three of these qualities. Variations in value are also called tints and shades, a tint being a red or other hue mixed with white, a shade being mixed with black. A large selection of these various colors is shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Shades_of_Red.svg/330px-Shades_of_Red.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_red","wikidata":"Q7460345"},{"title":"Bittersweet (Fuel song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Bittersweet\" is a song by American alternative rock band Fuel. It was released in November 1998 as the second single from their debut studio album, Sunburn."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9a/Fuel_bittersweet.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bittersweet_(Fuel_song)","wikidata":"Q16842539"},{"title":"List of Crayola crayon